IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `eia-core-insurable-employment`
IMPORT `ei5-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei5-agreement`
IMPORT `ei5-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer ei5-seat (Act Part VII.1). At least one case for every exported question, each in the facts a
-- real person in the seat would state. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Act (the section is named
-- beside the case), never copied from the module's own output. Dollar figures, rates and dates are invented for the cases.
-- Calendar facts used: 2026-06-07 and 2026-03-08 are Sundays; 2026-10-24 is a Saturday.
-- Arguments follow the order of the GIVEN of each question in ei5-seat.l4.

§ `Am I within this Part? (ss 152.01 and 152.02)`

-- Q: a freelance designer: a profession, not employed, no Part VIII, no s 5(4)(c) inclusion: a self-employed person (paragraph (a))
#ASSERT `Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of Part VII.1` `ei5 business - a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
-- a fisher to whom Part VIII regulations apply is taken out of the definition
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of Part VII.1` `ei5 business - a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE)
-- an employee who controls 60% of the voting shares of the corporation that employs them (paragraph (b), s 5(2)(b))
#ASSERT `Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of Part VII.1` `ei5 business - an employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0.6 FALSE FALSE
-- exactly 40% control is not "more than 40%": not within paragraph (b)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of Part VII.1` `ei5 business - an employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0.4 FALSE FALSE)

-- Q: self-employed earnings: a profession with income 30000, losses 2000 and 500 of excluded employment income: 30000 - 2000 + 500
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` `ei5 business - a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 30000 30000 FALSE 60000 0 2000 500 0 EQUALS JUST 28500
-- an Indian on a reserve: the income computed without reference to paragraph 81(1)(a) counts: 35000, not 20000
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` `ei5 business - a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 20000 35000 TRUE 60000 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 35000
-- a business that is more than half rent is left out: income 12000 of a rental business (rent 60 of 100): 0, less losses 1000
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` `ei5 business - a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 12000 12000 FALSE 100 60 1000 0 0 EQUALS JUST (0 MINUS 1000)
-- both paragraphs: a business (income 10000) and a controlled-corporation employment (insurable earnings it would have had: 4000)
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` `ei5 business - a trade` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0.5 10000 10000 FALSE 20000 0 0 0 4000 EQUALS JUST 14000
-- neither paragraph (an employee of an ordinary employer): not a self-employed person, so not covered
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` `ei5 business - an employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q: balance-due day for 2025: April 30, 2026; if the person died on 20 December 2025, six months after: 20 June 2026
#ASSERT `What is my balance-due day for the year` 2025 FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `What is my balance-due day for the year` 2025 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20

-- Q: Part VII.1 applies to a self-employed citizen who has entered into an agreement
#ASSERT `Does Part VII.1 apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Does Part VII.1 apply to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Part VII.1 apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `Is my agreement in the form and on the conditions the Commission has fixed` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my agreement in the form and on the conditions the Commission has fixed` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my agreement deemed to be terminated` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my agreement deemed to be terminated` FALSE)

-- Q: notice in writing before any benefits are paid
#ASSERT `May I terminate my agreement by giving notice to the Commission` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- benefits already paid and no prescribed circumstance: no
#ASSERT NOT (`May I terminate my agreement by giving notice to the Commission` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Q: agreement entered into on 10 January 2026, notice given in writing on 1 June 2026, nothing else happened: ends 31 December 2026
#ASSERT `What becomes of my notice to terminate the agreement` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `ei5 notice - the agreement terminates on December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`
-- notice on 11 March 2026, the 60th day after the agreement: deemed never entered into
#ASSERT `What becomes of my notice to terminate the agreement` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `ei5 notice - given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into, so the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into`
-- a benefit period was established on 1 September 2026 after the notice of 1 June: the notice is deemed never given
#ASSERT `What becomes of my notice to terminate the agreement` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `ei5 notice - deemed never to have been given, a benefit period having been established`
-- withdrawn on 1 December 2026
#ASSERT `What becomes of my notice to terminate the agreement` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 12 1) EQUALS `ei5 notice - withdrawn in the prescribed manner before December 31`

-- Q: the day on which the agreement terminates: the notice ends it on 31 December 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does my agreement terminate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `ei5 notice - the agreement terminates on December 31 of the year in which the notice was given` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31)
-- no notice that ends it and no deemed termination: it does not terminate
#ASSERT `On what day does my agreement terminate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `ei5 notice - not given in accordance with subsection (4), so the agreement is not terminated by it` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q: in force on 30 December 2026 but not on 31 December, when it terminates
#ASSERT `Is my agreement in force on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 12 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my agreement in force on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT `Is my agreement in force on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2040 1 1)

§ `If I cannot work because of an illness, injury or quarantine (s 152.03)`

-- Q: ill and unable to work, ceased to work because of it and would otherwise be working
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to benefits because of an illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- on parental benefits, did not stop work for the illness and would not be working anyway: still entitled (1.1)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to benefits because of an illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- would be deemed not to be working even without the illness: s 152.03(4) takes the entitlement away
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to benefits because of an illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- Q: 500 a week, a provincial law pays for the same reason, regulations reduce by 120: 380; no provincial benefit: 500
#ASSERT `How much of my weekly benefit remains after the reduction for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 TRUE 120 EQUALS 380
#ASSERT `How much of my weekly benefit remains after the reduction for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 FALSE 120 EQUALS 500
-- Q: 500 less 120 of plan allowances
#ASSERT `How much of my weekly benefit remains after deducting allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` 500 120 EQUALS 380

§ `If I am pregnant (s 152.04)`

#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me because of my pregnancy` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me because of my pregnancy` FALSE)
-- Q: confinement expected on Wednesday 10 June 2026 and not yet occurred: 15 March to 10 October 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my pregnancy benefits begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my pregnancy benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 10 10
-- the baby came late, on 1 July 2026: the period ends 31 October
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my pregnancy benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 10 31
-- (3.1) the week before the period is treated as part of it for the waiting period: 8 March 2026
#ASSERT `From which day is my pregnancy period treated as running for serving my waiting period` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 10 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
-- (5) and (6) three weeks in hospital: the period ends three weeks later, 31 October 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does my pregnancy benefit period end if my child is in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 10 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) 3 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 10 31

§ `If I am caring for a new-born or adopted child (s 152.05)`

#ASSERT `Are parental benefits payable to me for the care of a child` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Are parental benefits payable to me for the care of a child` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are parental benefits payable to me for the care of a child` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does my claim meet the requirement to elect the 35-week or the 61-week maximum` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my claim meet the requirement to elect the 35-week or the 61-week maximum` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my election of the 35-week or the 61-week maximum irrevocable` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my election of the 35-week or the 61-week maximum irrevocable` FALSE FALSE)
-- Q: I elected 35 weeks, the other parent (claiming first) elected 61: the first claimant's election binds both
#ASSERT `Which election of the maximum number of weeks binds me` `the 35-week maximum` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
-- I claimed first: mine binds
#ASSERT `Which election of the maximum number of weeks binds me` `the 35-week maximum` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE EQUALS `the 35-week maximum`
-- the other has not claimed
#ASSERT `Which election of the maximum number of weeks binds me` `the 35-week maximum` FALSE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS `the 35-week maximum`
-- Q: born on Wednesday 10 June 2026: 7 June 2026 to 12 June 2027
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my parental benefits begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 7
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my parental benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 12
-- four weeks in hospital: 10 July 2027
#ASSERT `On what day does my parental benefit period end if my child or children are in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) 4 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 7 10

-- Q: during the benefit period benefits were paid for two reasons (maximum total 87 weeks, more than 50), 10 weeks for the care of
-- a child under the 61-week maximum: the period is extended so benefits can be paid up to 61 weeks (s 152.05(5))
#ASSERT `Is my parental benefit period extended so that I can be paid up to the maximum` 2 87 10 61
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my parental benefit period extended so that I can be paid up to the maximum` 1 87 10 61)
-- 61 - 10 = 51 more weeks
#ASSERT `How many more weeks of parental benefits can I be paid after the extension` 2 87 10 61 EQUALS 51
#ASSERT `How many more weeks of parental benefits can I be paid after the extension` 1 87 10 61 EQUALS 0
-- only the 61-week parental benefit was paid: the period is extended by 26 weeks (s 152.05(5.1))
#ASSERT `By how many weeks is my parental benefit period extended if I was paid only parental benefits under the 61-week maximum` FALSE TRUE `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `By how many weeks is my parental benefit period extended if I was paid only parental benefits under the 61-week maximum` TRUE TRUE `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 0
-- the limits of (6) and (7)
#ASSERT `How long may my parental benefit period be after an extension under subsection (5)` 70 80 EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `How long may my parental benefit period be after an extension under subsection (5)` 90 80 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `How long may my parental benefit period be after an extension under subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1)` 105 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `How long may my parental benefit period be after an extension under subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1)` 90 EQUALS 90
-- (12), (13), (13.01): 40 or 69 weeks to divide, 35 or 61 to each
#ASSERT `How many weeks of parental benefits can be divided between me and another claimant` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `How many weeks of parental benefits can be divided between me and another claimant` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 69
#ASSERT `What is the most weeks of parental benefits I can be paid whatever the division` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `What is the most weeks of parental benefits I can be paid whatever the division` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 61
-- we elected 35 weeks: 20 and 20 are within; 30 and 11 are over 40
#ASSERT `Is our division of the weeks of parental benefits within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 20 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our division of the weeks of parental benefits within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 30 11)
#ASSERT `How many weeks of parental benefits will I be paid after the division` TRUE 30 20 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `How many weeks of parental benefits will I be paid after the division` FALSE 30 20 EQUALS 20
-- (14) my partner claimed for the same child and served the waiting period
#ASSERT `May I have my waiting period deferred because of my claim for a child` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I have my waiting period deferred because of my claim for a child` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (15)(a) my partner claims under section 23 and served the waiting period; I did not
#ASSERT `Am I not required to serve a waiting period because another person claiming under section 22 or 23 has served or elected to serve theirs` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not required to serve a waiting period because another person claiming under section 22 or 23 has served or elected to serve theirs` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `If I am caring for a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult (ss 152.06, 152.061 and 152.062)`

-- the certificate: a doctor; a foreign practitioner in the circumstances of reg 41.2; a foreign practitioner when the person is in Canada
#ASSERT `May this practitioner issue my certificate` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May this practitioner issue my certificate` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May this practitioner issue my certificate` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Q: a family member with a serious condition and a significant risk of death within 26 weeks, needing care
#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a gravely ill family member` TRUE TRUE TRUE 26 TRUE FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a gravely ill family member` TRUE TRUE TRUE 27 TRUE FALSE 0)
-- a prescribed shorter period of 12 weeks: 13 weeks of risk is too long
#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a gravely ill family member` TRUE TRUE TRUE 12 TRUE TRUE 12
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a gravely ill family member` TRUE TRUE TRUE 13 TRUE TRUE 12)
#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a critically ill child` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a critically ill child` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a critically ill adult` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me for the care or support of a critically ill adult` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Do I need another certificate for benefits payable after the first 26 weeks of compassionate care` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I need another certificate for benefits payable after the first 26 weeks of compassionate care` TRUE
-- the exception: all benefits already exhausted when the certificate is filed
#ASSERT `Does the exception apply so that my claim is not treated as made before my certificate was issued` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception apply so that my claim is not treated as made before my certificate was issued` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Q: first certificate issued Wednesday 11 March 2026, claim not made first: the period begins Sunday 8 March 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
-- claimed first, certified from Tuesday 24 February: the week of Sunday 22 February
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 22
-- the same but the exception applies: the week of the certificate again
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) TRUE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
-- the 52 weeks end on Saturday 6 March 2027
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE 0 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 6
-- benefits exhausted in the week of 10 June 2026: Saturday 13 June
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE 0 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 13
-- the person I care for died on Thursday 14 May 2026: Saturday 16 May
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 14) FALSE 0 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 16
-- a shorter period of 12 weeks prescribed for compassionate care: Saturday 30 May 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does the period for my caring benefits end` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 24) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE 12 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 30
#ASSERT `May I have my waiting period deferred because another claimant is claiming for the same person` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I have my waiting period deferred because another claimant is claiming for the same person` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- division of the remaining weeks: 26 for a family member, 35 for a critically ill child, 15 for an adult
#ASSERT `Is our division of the remaining weeks of caring benefits within the maximum` `care or support of a family member` 20 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our division of the remaining weeks of caring benefits within the maximum` `care or support of a family member` 20 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is our division of the remaining weeks of caring benefits within the maximum` `care or support of a critically ill child` 35 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our division of the remaining weeks of caring benefits within the maximum` `care or support of a critically ill adult` 8 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the pregnancy reason has no such maximum: not covered
#ASSERT `Is our division of the remaining weeks of caring benefits within the maximum` `pregnancy` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many weeks of caring benefits will I be paid after the division` TRUE 14 12 EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `How many weeks of caring benefits will I be paid after the division` FALSE 14 12 EQUALS 12
-- (10): compassionate care benefits are not payable for the child during the child's period (8 March 2026 to 6 March 2027)
#ASSERT `Are compassionate care benefits not payable to me in respect of this child or adult on this day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 6) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are compassionate care benefits not payable to me in respect of this child or adult on this day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 6) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 7))
-- (10.1) the 52 weeks from 8 March 2026 end on 6 March 2027
#ASSERT `Are critically ill adult benefits not payable to me on this day because I was paid for the critically ill child` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are critically ill adult benefits not payable to me on this day because I was paid for the critically ill child` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 7))

§ `Do I qualify for benefits? (ss 152.07 to 152.09)`

-- Q: entered into the agreement on 10 January 2026: twelve months expire on 10 January 2027
#ASSERT `Have at least 12 months expired since I entered into my agreement` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) FALSE 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have at least 12 months expired since I entered into my agreement` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 9) FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- a prescribed period of 6 months
#ASSERT `Have at least 12 months expired since I entered into my agreement` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 10) TRUE 6 FALSE
-- the Regulations deem me to have satisfied it (reg 76.43)
#ASSERT `Have at least 12 months expired since I entered into my agreement` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) FALSE 0 TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my agreement still in place, neither terminated nor deemed terminated` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my agreement still in place, neither terminated nor deemed terminated` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Have I had an interruption of earnings from self-employment` TRUE
-- Q: a benefit period beginning 4 January 2026, no amount fixed by regulation and no violation: $6,000
#ASSERT `How much self-employed earnings must I have had during my qualifying period` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 EQUALS 6000
-- with a serious violation in the 260 weeks: 6000 x 1.5
#ASSERT `How much self-employed earnings must I have had during my qualifying period` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) FALSE 0 TRUE `a serious violation` FALSE 0 EQUALS 9000
-- a benefit period beginning 2 May 2021: $5,000; with a minor violation 5000 x 1.25
#ASSERT `How much self-employed earnings must I have had during my qualifying period` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 2) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `How much self-employed earnings must I have had during my qualifying period` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 2) FALSE 0 TRUE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 EQUALS 6250
-- exactly the amount needed is enough; a dollar less is not
#ASSERT `Did I have enough self-employed earnings during my qualifying period` 6000 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I have enough self-employed earnings during my qualifying period` 5999 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0)
-- Q: do I qualify: agreement of 10 January 2024, claim on 1 March 2026, in place, an interruption, benefit period from 1 March, no violation, 7000 earned
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for benefits` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 7000
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for benefits` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 5000)
-- agreement only 6 months old
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for benefits` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE `a minor violation` FALSE 0 7000)
-- a serious violation raises the amount to 9000, so 7000 is not enough
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for benefits` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 TRUE `a serious violation` FALSE 0 7000)
-- Q: a violation of 1 May 2024 is within the 260 weeks before a claim of 1 March 2026; one of 1 January 2020 is not
#ASSERT `Was a violation accumulated in the 260 weeks before I made my initial claim` (YearMonthDay 2024 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was a violation accumulated in the 260 weeks before I made my initial claim` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1))

#ASSERT `Have I accumulated a violation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I accumulated a violation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Q: an overpayment of 1200, disentitled, a rate of 400 over an average of 10 weeks, at most 3000 could have been paid: 1200 + 3000
#ASSERT `What is the value of my violation` 1200 TRUE FALSE 400 10 3000 EQUALS 4200
-- Q: class by value and by an earlier violation
#ASSERT `What class is my violation` FALSE 999.99 (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS JUST `a minor violation`
#ASSERT `What class is my violation` FALSE 5000 (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS JUST `a very serious violation`
-- another violation on 1 June 2024: the notice of 1 June 2026 is within 260 weeks of it
#ASSERT `What class is my violation` FALSE 100 (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) EQUALS JUST `a subsequent violation`
-- a warning leaves it without a class
#ASSERT `What class is my violation` TRUE 100 (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day is my violation under section 7.1 treated as accumulated under Part VII.1` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3)
#ASSERT `On what day is my violation under section 7.1 treated as accumulated under Part VII.1` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May my violation be taken into account in this initial claim` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`May my violation be taken into account in this initial claim` 2)
-- Q: a benefit period beginning 4 January 2026: the qualifying period is the year 2025
#ASSERT `On what day does my qualifying period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 1 1
#ASSERT `On what day does my qualifying period end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 4) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `May my self-employed earnings of that year count for this initial claim` 0
#ASSERT NOT (`May my self-employed earnings of that year count for this initial claim` 1)
-- qualifies under both Parts: must elect
#ASSERT `Must I elect whether benefits are paid under Part VII.1 or Part I` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I elect whether benefits are paid under Part VII.1 or Part I` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Under which Part will my benefits be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE `Part VII.1` EQUALS JUST `Part VII.1`
-- qualifies under both and made no election: not decided
#ASSERT `Under which Part will my benefits be paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE `Part I` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under which Part will my benefits be paid` TRUE FALSE FALSE `Part I` EQUALS JUST `Part VII.1`
#ASSERT `Is my election binding for this reason` `pregnancy`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my election binding for this reason` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`)

§ `My benefit period (ss 152.1 to 152.12)`

#ASSERT `Will a benefit period be established for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- a prior benefit period has not ended
#ASSERT NOT (`Will a benefit period be established for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Are benefits payable to me for this week` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are benefits payable to me for this week` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Q: interruption of earnings on Wednesday 10 June 2026, claim on Wednesday 17 June: the later Sunday, 14 June
#ASSERT `When does my benefit period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 14
-- Q: late initial claim regarded as made on 1 April 2026
#ASSERT `On what day is my initial claim for benefits regarded as having been made` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1
-- no good cause shown, but the 2021 $5,000 amount is good cause by (5.1)
#ASSERT `On what day is my initial claim for benefits regarded as having been made` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1
#ASSERT `On what day is my initial claim for benefits regarded as having been made` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 17
#ASSERT `On what day is my other claim for benefits regarded as having been made` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 20
#ASSERT `On what day is my other claim for benefits regarded as having been made` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 17
#ASSERT `Is the lateness of my claim excused because the 2021 amount of $5,000 would not have let me qualify` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the lateness of my claim excused because the 2021 amount of $5,000 would not have let me qualify` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the exception apply so that my caring claim is not treated as made on an earlier day` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception apply so that my caring claim is not treated as made on an earlier day` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the Commission cancel my benefit period because it has ended with no benefits paid` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Commission cancel my benefit period because it has ended with no benefits paid` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the Commission cancel the part of my benefit period before my first week of benefits at my request` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Commission cancel the part of my benefit period before my first week of benefits at my request` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (8) a cancelled benefit period is deemed never to have begun; one that has not been cancelled is not
#ASSERT `Is my cancelled benefit period treated as never having begun` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my cancelled benefit period treated as never having begun` FALSE)
-- Q: requested 1 May, new claim 15 May, qualified 10 May: the last of the three is 15 May
#ASSERT `On what day have I requested the end of my benefit period, made a new initial claim and qualified` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15)
#ASSERT `On what day have I requested the end of my benefit period, made a new initial claim and qualified` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q: a benefit period that begins 14 June 2026 and is 52 weeks long ends on Saturday 12 June 2027
#ASSERT `On what day does my benefit period end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 14) 52 FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 12
-- no further benefits payable from 1 March 2027
#ASSERT `On what day does my benefit period end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 14) 52 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 1
